which by substituting  $\vec{PQ} = \vec{Q}-\vec{P}$  yields
\begin{align*}
&(\vec{B}-\vec{A})^2 = (\vec{C}-\vec{B})^2 \iff \vec{A}\cdot\vec{A}+\vec{B}\cdot\vec{B}-2\cdot\vec{A}\cdot\vec{B} = \vec{B}\cdot\vec{B}+\vec{C}\cdot\vec{C}-2\cdot\vec{B}\cdot\vec{C} \iff \vec{A}\cdot\vec{A}-2\cdot\vec{A}\cdot\vec{B} = \vec{C}\cdot\vec{C}-2\cdot\vec{B}\cdot\vec{C} 
&(\vec{D}-\vec{C})^2 = (\vec{E}-\vec{D})^2 \iff \vec{C}\cdot\vec{C}+\vec{D}\cdot\vec{D}-2\cdot\vec{C}\cdot\vec{D} = \vec{D}\cdot\vec{D}+\vec{E}\cdot\vec{E}-2\cdot\vec{D}\cdot\vec{E} \iff \vec{C}\cdot\vec{C}-2\cdot\vec{C}\cdot\vec{D} = \vec{E}\cdot\vec{E}-2\cdot\vec{D}\cdot\vec{E} 
&(\vec{F}-\vec{E})^2 = (\vec{A}-\vec{F})^2 \iff \vec{E}\cdot\vec{E}+\vec{F}\cdot\vec{F}-2\cdot\vec{E}\cdot\vec{F} = \vec{F}\cdot\vec{F}+\vec{A}\cdot\vec{A}-2\cdot\vec{F}\cdot\vec{A} \iff \vec{E}\cdot\vec{E}-2\cdot\vec{E}\cdot\vec{F} = \vec{A}\cdot\vec{A}-2\cdot\vec{F}\cdot\vec{A}.
\end{align*}
Summing,  $$ \vec{A}\cdot\vec{A}+\vec{C}\cdot\vec{C}+\vec{E}\cdot\vec{E}-2\cdot\vec{A}\cdot\vec{B}-2\cdot\vec{C}\cdot\vec{D}-2\cdot\vec{E}\cdot\vec{F}=\vec{C}\cdot\vec{C}+\vec{E}\cdot\vec{E}+\vec{A}\cdot\vec{A}-2\cdot\vec{B}\cdot\vec{C}-2\cdot\vec{D}\cdot\vec{E}-2\cdot\vec{F}\cdot\vec{A}, $$  and cancelling out  $\vec{E}\cdot\vec{E}+\vec{A}\cdot\vec{A}+\vec{C}\cdot\vec{C}$  and dividing by  $2$  gives  $$ -\vec{A}\cdot\vec{B}-\vec{C}\cdot\vec{D}-\vec{E}\cdot\vec{F} = -\vec{B}\cdot\vec{C}-\vec{D}\cdot\vec{E}-\vec{F}\cdot\vec{A} \iff \vec{B}\cdot\vec{C}+\vec{D}\cdot\vec{E}+\vec{F}\cdot\vec{A}-\vec{A}\cdot\vec{B}-\vec{C}\cdot\vec{D}-\vec{E}\cdot\vec{F} = 0.\qquad(\ast) $$  Next, the magical point of concurrency. Let the perpendiculars from  $C$  and  $E$  to segments  $BD$  and  $DF$  intersect at  $X$ , so that  $\overline{BD}\perp\overline{CX}$  and  $\overline{DF}\perp\overline{EX}$ , i.e.,
\begin{align*}
& \vec{BD}\cdot\vec{CX} = (\vec{D}-\vec{B})\cdot(\vec{X}-\vec{C}) = \vec{B}\cdot\vec{C}+\vec{D}\cdot\vec{X}-\vec{B}\cdot\vec{X}-\vec{C}\cdot\vec{D} = 0 
& \vec{DF}\cdot\vec{EX} = (\vec{F}-\vec{D})\cdot(\vec{X}-\vec{E}) = \vec{D}\cdot\vec{E}+\vec{F}\cdot\vec{X}-\vec{D}\cdot\vec{X}-\vec{E}\cdot\vec{F} = 0.
\end{align*}
Summing,  $$ (\vec{B}\cdot\vec{C}+\vec{D}\cdot\vec{E})+(\vec{D}\cdot\vec{X}+\vec{F}\cdot\vec{X})-(\vec{B}\cdot\vec{X}+\vec{D}\cdot\vec{X})+(\vec{C}\cdot\vec{D}+\vec{E}\cdot\vec{F}) = 0.\qquad(\dagger) $$  Something about the above equation looks eerily familiar... 

Going back to  $(\ast)$ , if we add  $(\vec{D}\cdot\vec{X}+\vec{F}\cdot\vec{X}+\vec{B}\cdot\vec{X})-(\vec{B}\cdot\vec{X}+\vec{D}\cdot\vec{X}+\vec{F}\cdot\vec{X}) = 0$ , we have that  $$ (\vec{B}\cdot\vec{C}+\vec{D}\cdot\vec{E}+\vec{F}\cdot\vec{A})+(\vec{D}\cdot\vec{X}+\vec{F}\cdot\vec{X}+\vec{B}\cdot\vec{X})-(\vec{B}\cdot\vec{X}+\vec{D}\cdot\vec{X}+\vec{F}\cdot\vec{X})-(\vec{A}\cdot\vec{B}+\vec{C}\cdot\vec{D}+\vec{E}\cdot\vec{F}) = 0. $$  Aha! Subtracting  $(\dagger)$  from this new  $(\ast)$  yields  $$ \vec{F}\cdot\vec{A}+\vec{B}\cdot\vec{X}-\vec{F}\cdot\vec{X}-\vec{A}\cdot\vec{B} = (\vec{B}-\vec{F})\cdot(\vec{X}-\vec{A}) = \vec{FB}\cdot\vec{AX} = 0, $$  which implies that  $\overline{FB}\perp\overline{AX}$ , the requested result.  $\blacksquare$

